A||||3||Guy||Wiring (connection)Problem||||1||
Z||000000||Guy||11-25-2000||08:07 AM||||My trouble is in the wiring to the temperature gauge. During warm-up, the gauge moves slowly from one end to the other as it reaches the high end, the warning lamp also comes on. The problem vaires with outside temperature !! When it is hot - the problem is often not there. But as the days get cooler, the gauge mis behaves all the time and for longer periods. Yesterday - it was below zero and the gauge waved back and forth for 30 minutes. And after then it always settles down. Now- I have checked the fluid levels, changed the sensor, did the resistor checks, etc and it all points to a loss or corroded connection (high resistance) problem. I checked the connections at the wiring point beside the battery and redid those as well as those in the instrument panel. <P>Does anyone else have any idea's on how to trouble shoot this suspected high resistance problem ? <P>In my old telephone company days, we had a "breakdown" set which would break high resistance connections - but I do not have access to one nor would it be a good idea for electronics.<P>Cheers,<P>Guy<P>87' GT 3.1||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||11-25-2000||10:06 AM||||One quick test that I can think of- ground both wires at the sensor connector and see if the gage and light act normally. The gage should immediately peg and of course the light should come on. Then ground  the gage at the dash and check the operation.  That should at least narrow it down||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||11-25-2000||12:23 PM||||Agree with Phil's suggestion.  In addition, might test the sending unit by sticking it in boiling water (need to attach a ground to it!).  Yes, I did this one time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> , to calibrate the dash gage (needle fell off!).  But actually, at this point I'm not even sure if we're talking about the OE Fiero sending unit....   <P>Says in your signature, "'87 GT 3.1."  Does the car we're talking about have a 3.1 in it?  The 3.1's are tricky to get all the air out, and that has caused my gage to do weird things.  Some 3.1's have a little plug on the water outlet you have to remove, while you fill the cooling system.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000003||theogre||11-25-2000||03:23 PM||||Check all the ground on the block. one of them may be loose. ||||reg||1
